  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Isotropic 3D electron microscopy data of isolated murine pancreatic islets treated with low glucose (jrc_mus-pancreas-2) (2022) in Figshare. 2 citations.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Isotropic 3D electron microscopy data of isolated murine pancreatic islets treated with low glucose (jrc_mus-pancreas-2) (2022) in Figshare is authored by Technology Group, FIB-SEM, Mueller, Andreas and Solimena, Michele. Topics: Islet, Chemistry, Pancreatic islets, Ultrastructure and Acetone.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">2 citations (OpenAlex). Citations peaked in 2023 with 1 citing works. Citing venues include bioRxiv (Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory) and Nature Communications.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Limited online visibility beyond citations.</p>",
  "provenance": {},
  "story_type": "DataStory",
  "publisher": "Digital Science",
  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This 2022 Figshare dataset has an early but meaningful reuse profile: it is linked to 2 citations, 3 documented downstream reuses, and reuse in both a preprint and a journal article. The record suggests the dataset is being taken up in a focused research network around pancreatic islet biology and beta-cell structure.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This dataset provides isotropic 3D electron microscopy data from isolated murine pancreatic islets treated with low glucose, supporting ultrastructural analysis of pancreatic islet organization and secretion-related biology. Its impact record is still small in absolute terms, but the available signals point to concrete scientific reuse rather than isolated storage alone.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The clearest evidence of uptake is scholarly citation. OpenAlex records 2 citations, one in 2023 and one in 2024, showing that the dataset has already entered the literature. The citing works span a preprint and a peer-reviewed article, both on beta-cell primary cilia, which indicates that the data are being used in active, closely related investigations rather than only in distant secondary contexts.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Reuse signals reinforce that picture. DataCite and related reuse tracking identify 3 downstream reuses, including an associated article, and Crossref data-citation records show the dataset being referenced explicitly by both the 2023 preprint and the 2024 Nature Communications article. Taken together, these signals suggest the dataset is contributing to a sustained line of inquiry in pancreatic function and diabetes research.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">At the same time, the surrounding attention record is sparse. There are no recorded online mentions in Event Data, no scite citation classifications, and no downloadable or viewable usage recorded by DataCite. In other words, the evidence shows early scholarly incorporation, but not broad public engagement. This is consistent with a specialized dataset whose value is emerging through targeted reuse within a well-defined research community.</p>",
  "narrative_source": "template"
